{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And if men strive.</b> The Gaon [Saadia] said <b>with a stone</b> is like <b>with the fist</b>. And Rabbi Marinus said that the alef is added, like the alef in אזרועי (Job 31:22), from the root גרפם (Judges 5:21), a thing one grasps in his hand, and likewise in the Arabic language."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {0 "The Hebrew text is garbled: the lemma head reads 'וכי יריבן' (v. 18) but the comment immediately discusses 'באגרוף' (v. 19), while the Gaon's gloss 'כמו בעלי אגרופין' is followed by a Talmudic citation (Sanhedrin 49a) and what appears to be a stray phrase 'דבר חזק וקשה.' I have translated the lemma as given and preserved the disjointed sequence exactly."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:36:57.926988870Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}